  "title": "HawkSet: Automatic, Application-Agnostic, and Efficient Concurrent PM Bug Detection",
  "abstract": "Persistent Memory (PM) enables the development of fast, persistent applications without employing costly HDD/SSD-based I/O operations. Since caches are volatile and CPUs may reorder and stall memory accesses for performance, developers must use low-level instructions to ensure a consistent state in case of a crash. Failure to do so can result in data corruption, data loss, or undefined behavior. In concurrent executions, this exposes a new class of bugs.",
  "abstract_source_id": "src-abstract-eurosys-2025-a439be38",
